=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

File 1: internal/tesla/router/writers/charging_telemetry_writer.go
  - Per Decision #1: NewChargingTelemetryWriter(pool *pgxpool.Pool) router.Writer
    Panics on nil pool with "NewChargingTelemetryWriter: pool must
    be non-nil" — same fail-fast pattern as NewClimateWriter,
    NewSafetyWriter, NewMediaWriter. Wrapped snapshotWriter
    constructor errors panic with the wrapped error in the message.
  - Per Decision #2: composes newSnapshotWriter(pool,
    "charging_telemetry", chargingTelemetryColumnFor). The (vehicle_id,
    ts) PK upsert pattern from snapshot_base.go works for time-series
    too because charging_telemetry's PK matches the *_snapshots PK
    shape, and two atomics for the same tick coalesce into one row
    with both columns set — exactly the ~1 Hz sampling contract from
    migration 000184:111-112.
  - Per Decision #3: writer NEVER touches session_id. snapshot_base.go's
    INSERT column list is (vehicle_id, ts, <col>) where <col> is
    sourced from chargingTelemetryColumnByField, so session_id is
    omitted from BOTH the INSERT and the ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET
    clause — the FK survives across per-column re-deliveries. The
    map's godoc explicitly references the 0030 session tracker as the
    backfill source.
  - Per Decision #4 (map source): chargingTelemetryColumnByField is
    a static var — 12 entries copied verbatim from routing.yaml's
    `dest: charging_telemetry` block; the godoc cites the
    AUDIT_EVIDENCE Check 2 enumeration for verifiability.
  - All 12 codec.Atomic.Value kinds (7 float64, 1 int64, 2 bool, 2
    string) are covered by snapshot_base.go's bindSnapshotValue at
    lines 194-209; no TIMESTAMPTZ hybrid wrapper needed (cf.
    tire_pressure_writer.go's writeTimestamp seam) because no
    charging_telemetry column is TIMESTAMPTZ.

File 2: internal/tesla/router/writers/charging_telemetry_writer_test.go
  - Per Decision #5 (reflective coverage):
    TestChargingTelemetryWriter_ColumnMapMatchesRoutingYAML calls
    router.LoadMap(), filters by Destination == DestChargingTelemetry,
    asserts count == 12, and asserts the writer map matches
    entry-for-entry. Catches three drift classes (missing-in-writer,
    extra-in-writer, column-name-mismatch).
  - Per Decision #6 (per-kind positives):
    TestChargingTelemetryWriter_TypeMatrix exercises one positive
    write per scalar kind: float64 (ACChargingPower), int64
    (ChargerPhases), bool (BatteryHeaterOn), text (FastChargerType).
    All four scalar kinds the helper handles are touched because
    charging_telemetry has columns of all four types.
  - Per Decision #6 (assert session_id NULL on insert):
    TestChargingTelemetryWriter_SessionIDNotTouched iterates EVERY
    routed field, sends a Write with a kind-appropriate value, and
    asserts the rendered SQL does NOT contain the substring
    "session_id". Per-field iteration (rather than one
    representative) defends against a future bug that affects only
    one column path.
  - Per Decision #6 (unknown-field):
    TestChargingTelemetryWriter_UnknownFieldReturnsError uses
    "VehicleSpeed" (a routed field for drive_telemetry) — defends
    against accidentally widening the charging_telemetry map to
    swallow non-charging fields. Asserts error wording and zero
    db.Exec calls.
  - TestNewChargingTelemetryWriter_NilPoolPanics locks Decision #1's
    fail-fast contract.

